       "text": "I entered the order as written: **amlodipine 50 mg by mouth once daily (Order ID ORD-0001)**.\n\nI attached a note to the order. It says 50 mg is 5 times the 10 mg daily maximum, that you were warned about the risk of severe low blood pressure and confirmed the dose, and that a pharmacist needs to verify it before it's dispensed. Pharmacy may contact you to confirm.\n\nIf the patient does get this dose, consider frequent blood pressure and heart rate checks and continuous heart monitoring. The drug stays in the body a long time, so effects could build up over several days. Watch for low blood pressure, fast heart rate, swelling, and fluid in the lungs.\n\nIf you need to change or cancel the order, tell me and I'll update it."
